{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01G3vvZH9ueDMuFSZS3W1vTA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VYBV66WVLwuQHbuRiE4vhq","name":"Agent","input":{"subagent_type":"claude","description":"Reviewer 2: Novelty + Related Work","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 in a full-mode dream review. Your scope: **novelty + related work + story consistency only**. Do NOT evaluate method implementation details or experimental design.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\"When Does Multivariate Conformal Prediction Help VLA Action Correction?\" — A diagnostic study testing whether multivariate conformal prediction (CP) features enable dimension-selective action correction in Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models. Central finding is negative: at K=10 samples and d=7 DOF, Ledoit-Wolf shrinkage intensity reaches 0.71, collapsing covariance toward identity and rendering per-DOF conformal features uninformative. System called ACR-VLA, tested on LIBERO-Plus.\n\nThis is the **worst** tier dream (maximally pessimistic narrative). Conflicts between narrative and evidence must be flagged.\n\n## Paper Details\n\n### Contributions (claimed):\n1. Identify K-vs-dimension failure mode for multivariate CP in VLA action correction; transition at shrinkage ~0.5 (K/d² ≈ 1).\n2. Comprehensive ablation (8 ablations, 11 conditions) showing 3.1pp improvement is from generic observation-conditioned residual, not conformal features.\n3. Online COC-driven ACI is ineffective due to denoising stochasticity dominating inter-chunk disagreement.\n\n### Related Work (Section 6):\n- **CP in robotics**: Lindemann et al. 2023 (trajectory prediction), Dixit et al. 2024 (policy gating), Luo et al. 2024 (sample selection). Paper claims to be \"first to systematically test multivariate CP features as learned correction module inputs.\"\n- **Learned residual correction**: A2C2 (Ankile et al. 2024), PLD (Shi et al. 2024). A3 ablation reproduces this in VLA setting.\n- **VLA robustness**: RobustVLA, DiG-Flow, SRPO. Stacking experiment shows diminishing returns.\n\n### Key Results:\n- Table 1: ACR-VLA full: 65.1% LIBERO-Plus (+3.1pp over base 62.0%), 93.7% nominal (−2.8pp).\n- Table 2: A3 (no conformal features) = 64.3%, full = 65.1%, gap = 0.8pp (within ~1.5pp noise). Scalar uncertainty A4 = 65.3% matches or beats 45D conformal.\n- Per-perturbation (Table 4): Gains correlate with training augmentation coverage, not uncertainty.\n- COC/ACI (Table 3): ρ=0.19 (FAIL), volume narrowing 6.2% (FAIL).\n- All uncertainty variants within 1.1pp of no-uncertainty baseline (Table 5).\n- SRPO stacking: +1.3pp, below 2pp significance.\n- Discussion proposes K/d² ≈ 1 as empirical threshold. 3-DOF synthetic validates (shrinkage 0.32, >5pp advantage).\n\n### References cited:\nAngelopoulos & Bates 2021, Ankile et al. 2024, Black et al. 2024, Dixit et al. 2024, Gibbs & Candès 2021, Ledoit & Wolf 2004, Lindemann et al. 2023, Luo et al. 2024, Pertsch et al. 2025, Shi et al. 2024, SRPO 2025 (anonymous), Vovk et al. 2005, Wen et al. 2025.\n\n## Your Review Tasks\n\nEvaluate:\n1. **Novelty**: Is the differentiation from existing work clear? Do the contribution claims stand independently?\n2. **Related work coverage**: Are important baselines missing? Is positioning accurate?\n3. **Story consistency**: Even in simulated data, does the argumentation logic hold? Do intro/abstract/conclusion claims match method/experiment evidence? Are there contradictions?\n\nFlag any conflicts with the \"worst\" tier narrative. If the paper over-claims or under-claims pessimism relative to evidence, note it.\n\nProvide your review in structured format with: (a) summary of strengths, (b) summary of weaknesses, (c) detailed issues with severity (major/minor), (d) your preliminary score (strong reject / borderline reject / borderline accept / weak accept / accept).\n\nRespond concisely — no pleasantries."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3046,"cache_read_input_tokens":41563,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3046},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"908704ee-979c-4338-9cc9-65d0350375b6","uuid":"9d78dfa8-777d-4086-b194-9f1e2e1a67bd"}
